Z||000005||JSocha||06-14-2001||02:17 AM||||Good morning Ross!  Long time no hear from! How was work this evening?  You must of just got home.  How bad did your part of town get hit by that hail storm on Saturday?  Hope all is well and it missed you!  Also hope you weren't out in your 88 GT at the time!<P>BTW, may have to ask your expertise or see who you might recommend based on my other thread about Diabetities as Frontal Lobe mentioned you.<P>And my Fiero is still in Minot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  Took the tranny over to him that I got from Strege Auto.  Turned out it wasn't a Muncie but an Izuzu tranny to which Strege was unaware of.  They went by the coding on the tranny.<P>So, ended up having them order the rebuilt because if I was going to dump that much money into a used might as well pay a couple hundred more for one that I know will last.<P>Car should be done by next weekend.||||reg||1
Z||000006||RossT||06-14-2001||02:45 AM||||Jeff, I just now read thru the other post. I normally nevery visit the OT sections, so I am glad I did tonight.  Sound like your very frustrated, but you are on the right track. Getting eductated and keeping the weight off is half the battle.<P>I am at work now. 0130 AM<P>All of Bismarck got nailed by the hail.  My wife was smart and put the new minivan in the garage before it hit.  My truck was outside and got some damage.  There was 3 feet of hail in some areas and even the snow plows got stuck trying to move it.  The old timers say it was the worst hail storm every for Bismarck.  But My fiero was safe in the garage.<P>My fiero won its class at the Wisconsin Dells Run!!<P>Now I know why you haven't posted much lately.<P>Let me know the RX's and I will let you know what I think.  Its always best to start one at time, but some of them work best together.<P>Ross||||reg||1
